ashboard titled 'LOC-2f351135 Web logs' with exactly 2 panels:\\n- Request count over time (date_histogram on timestamp, count)\\n- Request count by HTTP response code (terms on response, count)\\n\\nPanel 1: chart_type is line, data_view is 'Kibana Sample Data Logs', metrics [{agg: count}], group_by [{field: timestamp, kind: date_histogram}].\\n\\nPanel 2: chart_type is bar (or pie), metrics [{agg: count}], group_by [{field: response, kind: terms, limit: probably 10}]. Use bar.\\n\\nLet's create the dashboard.\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"message\", \"content\": \"Step 1 complete: the data view's time field is `timestamp`. Key fields include `response` (string, the HTTP response code) and `timestamp` (date).\\n\\nNow Step 2 — creating the dashboard with two panels:\\n\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"tool_call\", \"name\": \"create_dashboard\", \"arguments\": {\"title\": \"LOC-2f351135 Web logs\", \"panels\": [{\"title\": \"Requests over time\", \"chart_type\": \"line\", \"data_view\": \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\", \"metrics\": [{\"agg\": \"count\", \"label\": \"requests\"}], \"group_by\": [{\"field\": \"timestamp\", \"kind\": \"date_histogram\"}]}, {\"title\": \"Requests by response code\", \"chart_type\": \"bar\", \"data_view\": \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\", \"metrics\": [{\"agg\": \"count\", \"label\": \"requests\"}], \"group_by\": [{\"field\": \"response\", \"kind\": \"terms\", \"limit\": 20}]}]}}], \"finish_reason\": \"tool_call\"}]"}}, {"key": "agent.model.tool_calls", "value": {"intValue": "1"}}, {"key": "agent.model.thinking", "value": {"boolValue": true}}, {"key": "agent.model.finish_reason_inferred", "value": {"boolValue": true}}, {"key": "agent.secret.exposed", "value": {"boolValue": false}}], "status": {"code": 0}}, {"traceId": "5dafd8feb28c5cb3109d0a79af7fe389", "spanId": "f9cfa6c6eb282525", "parentSpanId": "833e053a3be84a99", "name": "chat qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "kind": 3, "startTimeUnixNano": "1791825596252661984", "endTimeUnixNano": "1791825671125161984", "attributes": [{"key"